    {
      "id": "p0022-b003",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "Cultures are basically their own giant in-groups: they have their own histories, customs, rituals, traditions, folk stories, foods, and more. A reference to any of these might sound meaningless to an outsider when translated literally. In this situation, understanding the literal words isn't enough - the actual \"inside joke\" needs to be explained too. It basically needs to be translated twice instead of only once.",
        "raw": "Cultures are basically their own giant in-groups: they have their own histories,\ncustoms, rituals, traditions, folk stories, foods, and more. A reference to any of\nthese might sound meaningless to an outsider when translated literally. In this\nsituation, understanding the literal words isn't enough - the actual \"inside joke\"\nneeds to be explained too. It basically needs to be translated twice instead of\nonly once.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.28574356,
          0.15908571,
          0.89560373,
          0.26337143
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.28326429,
          0.15837143,
          0.89762762,
          0.26444286
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          5,
          6,
          7,
          8,
          9,
          10
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "每种文化都像一个巨大的圈子，有自己的历史、习俗、仪式、传统、民间故事、食物等。提及其中任何一项，直译给圈外人听都可能毫无意义。这时，理解字面还不够，也得解释那个“圈内笑话”。相当于要翻译两遍，而不是一遍。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
